{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/query/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:11:35.270906Z","id":"cb61e706db9f37aa91f2864afc2d2d34f61c01b57bc64d5858892948a1a735e6","body":{"detail":"path_context (crates/path-cli/src/query/mod.rs:470-484) builds the `path` object attached to every step from `id`, `base` and `meta` only, and the `path query` help (crates/path-cli/src/cmd_query.rs:78) documents that shape. With path.parent in the format, 'which cached sessions continue or fork session X' is a natural jq filter (`map(select(.path.parent.path == \"X\"))`), but it always returns nothing because the field is never exposed. The doc comments at query/mod.rs:467-468 and cmd_query.rs:18 say 'the parent path's id/base/meta' meaning the path that contains the step; since path.parent now names a different path, that wording reads as the lineage parent.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":467},"end":{"line":484},"content_hash":"25db3ff9c46777d394cde4aeab0c27e6a64af0471c5d700661ab94f2a33ba3e0"},"suggested_fix":"Insert `parent` (serialized Parent) into path_context when set, list it in the cmd_query.rs help shape, and reword both comments to 'the containing path's id, base, parent and meta'.","summary":"path query's per-step path context carries id, base and meta but not path.parent, and its doc comment calls the containing path 'the parent path'","tags":["review","review:pr-354-qual-2","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/query/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:14:02.179489Z","id":"e80787301e11238a2808e920c64b6b8152c91bae3690e69fca1f3e7112e87ccc","body":{"detail":"crates/path-cli/src/query/mod.rs:469-486 path_context inserts only id, base and meta; doc comment at 467-468 says 'the parent path's id, base, and meta'. crates/path-cli/src/cmd_query.rs:17-18 repeats 'the parent path's id/base/meta' and the help shape at cmd_query.rs:78 lists only id/base/meta. So .path.parent is always absent from query output. suggestion is right.","kind":"comment","references":"cb61e706db9f37aa91f2864afc2d2d34f61c01b57bc64d5858892948a1a735e6","summary":"confirmed: path_context omits path.parent and its doc comments call the containing path 'the parent path'","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/query/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T18:57:37.959825Z","id":"d0de5a6e4d6ef9f382eaef55c907a89ba6df140f038fda56436ddaefee91bd8c","body":{"detail":"Owner approval, 2026-10-13. The path object copied onto each step is the path header; parent is now part of the header, so it goes in alongside base and meta. The doc comment stops calling the containing path 'the parent path'. Rides along in the #354 fix pass.","kind":"decision","references":"cb61e706db9f37aa91f2864afc2d2d34f61c01b57bc64d5858892948a1a735e6","suggested_fix":"In crates/path-cli/src/query/mod.rs path_context, insert \"parent\" when path.path.parent is Some, mirroring base; change the doc comment to 'the containing path's id, base, parent, and meta'; add a query test that a filter on .path.parent.path matches a path carrying a parent.","summary":"Decided: fix; add parent to the per-step path context and rename the containing path in the doc comment","tags":["review:pr-354-qual-2","decision","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/query/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T19:05:46.892488Z","id":"e1d870ed3bdf912b025c9f498719f8956f94bca07df80053220456565b2c50c7","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:90ed716","summary":"Fixed in 90ed716 on ben/path-parent: path_context inserts 'parent' when path.path.parent is Some, mirroring base; the doc comment says 'the containing path's id, base, parent, and meta'; cmd_query.rs doc comment and help shape list parent too. tests/query.rs filter_on_path_parent_finds_continuations passes: a filter on .path.parent.path == \"sess-1\" returns only the seeded continuation.","supersedes":"cb61e706db9f37aa91f2864afc2d2d34f61c01b57bc64d5858892948a1a735e6","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
